<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title><%= yield(:title).presence || "Remindly — spoken reminders for seniors, set up by the people who care for them" %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="description" content="<%= yield(:description).presence || "Remindly speaks reminders aloud at the right time, so a senior does not have to read a screen or open an app. Caregivers set them up from anywhere." %>">
    <link rel="canonical" href="<%= canonical_url %>">
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>

    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Remindly">
    <meta property="og:title" content="<%= yield(:title).presence || "Remindly — spoken reminders for seniors" %>">
    <meta property="og:description" content="<%= yield(:description).presence || "Spoken reminders for seniors, set up by the people who care for them." %>">
    <meta property="og:url" content="<%= canonical_url %>">

    <%#
      Shared links to this site are how most people will first hear of it, and a
      link with no image is rendered as a bare grey box by Facebook, LinkedIn,
      WhatsApp and iMessage alike. The absolute URL is required — these scrapers
      do not resolve relative paths — and it stays on CANONICAL_HOST so the card
      is identical no matter which of the three hostnames was shared.
    %>
    <meta property="og:image" content="<%= canonical_host %>/og-image.png">
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="Remindly — spoken reminders for a parent living on their own. Free to use.">
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">

    <%#
      Structured data. Pages opt in with content_for :structured_data; without it
      nothing is emitted, so a page that has nothing meaningful to declare does
      not ship an empty graph. Rendered as a JSON-LD data block, which browsers
      never execute — it exists for search engines.
    %>
    <% if content_for?(:structured_data) %>
      <script type="application/ld+json"><%= yield(:structured_data) %></script>
    <% end %>

    <%#
      Who publishes this site, on every page. Page-level graphs above say what a
      given page is; nothing said who is behind it, which is the association
      search engines use to tie a domain, a name and a support address together.
      Separate from the page graph deliberately — a page that declares nothing of
      its own still declares this.
    %>
    <script type="application/ld+json"><%= json_ld(
      "@context" => "https://schema.org",
      "@graph" => [
        {
          "@type" => "Organization",
          "@id" => "#{canonical_host}#organization",
          "name" => "Remindly",
          "url" => canonical_host,
          "email" => "hello@remindly.care",
          "description" => "Free spoken reminders for older people living on their own, set up by the family who care for them.",
          "logo" => "#{canonical_host}/icon.png"
        },
        {
          "@type" => "WebSite",
          "@id" => "#{canonical_host}#website",
          "name" => "Remindly",
          "url" => canonical_host,
          "publisher" => { "@id" => "#{canonical_host}#organization" },
          "inLanguage" => "en"
        }
      ]
    ) %></script>

    <%#
      Styles are inlined rather than linked. There is no asset pipeline in this app,
      the dashboard pulls Tailwind from a CDN (~400KB of JS that Tailwind itself
      warns against in production), and this is the one page meant to rank — so it
      should not block rendering on a third-party request. Small enough to read.
    %>
    <style>
      :root {
        --ink: #1f2933;
        --muted: #52606d;
        --line: #e4e7eb;
        --brand: #2f5bea;
        --brand-dark: #1e40af;
        --bg: #ffffff;
        --bg-soft: #f5f7fa;
      }

      *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--ink);
        font: 400 1.125rem/1.6 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      }

      .wrap { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.25rem; }

      header {
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
        padding: 1.25rem 0;
      }
      header .wrap { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; }
      .logo { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--brand); text-decoration: none; }

      h1 {
        font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.75rem);
        line-height: 1.15;
        margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      }
      h2 {
        font-size: 1.5rem;
        margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      }
      /* Until the landing page there was no h3 anywhere in prose — the only
         ones on the site are on the printable sheets, where .sheet-heading
         handles them. A run of questions under one h2 needs the level to be
         visible, and the browser default is bold body text tight against the
         paragraph above it. */
      h3 {
        font-size: 1.2rem;
        margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      }
      p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
      .lead { font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--muted); }

      .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; margin: 2rem 0 3rem; }

      /* Generous hit areas: some visitors here are the seniors themselves. */
      .btn {
        display: inline-block;
        padding: 0.9rem 1.5rem;
        border-radius: 0.6rem;
        /* font: inherit before font-weight — a <button> defaults to a smaller
           system font, so without this the button ones came out visibly
           smaller than the <a> ones sitting next to them. */
        font: inherit;
        font-weight: 600;
        text-decoration: none;
        border: 2px solid transparent;
        cursor: pointer;
      }
      .btn-primary { background: var(--brand); color: #fff; }
      .btn-primary:hover { background: var(--brand-dark); }
      .btn-secondary { border-color: var(--line); color: var(--ink); }
      .btn-secondary:hover { background: var(--bg-soft); }

      .btn:focus-visible, a:focus-visible {
        outline: 3px solid var(--brand);
        outline-offset: 2px;
      }

      .brand { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; }

      .top-nav {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 1.25rem;
        font-size: 1rem;
      }
      .top-nav a { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; }
      .top-nav a:hover { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: underline; }
      /* The one link that is an action rather than a destination. */
      .top-nav .nav-cta { color: var(--brand); font-weight: 600; }

      @media (max-width: 34rem) {
        /* Stack under the logo rather than squeezing beside it, so the heading
           does not get pushed off the first screen on a phone. */
        header .wrap { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.6rem; }
        .top-nav { gap: 1rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
      }

      /* Quiet on purpose. A loud badge on a product aimed at family caregivers
         — a group used to being sold to — reads as a hook rather than as
         generosity, and invites "what's the catch" instead of answering it. */
      .badge-free {
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--brand);
        background: var(--bg-soft);
        border: 1px solid var(--line);
        border-radius: 999px;
        padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
      }

      /* Sits directly under the call to action, so it reads as part of it.
         Bordered rather than muted grey: it was the least visible line on the
         page while carrying the fact most likely to earn the click. */
      .free-note {
        margin: -1rem 0 3rem;
        padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
        color: var(--muted);
        background: var(--bg-soft);
        border-left: 4px solid var(--brand);
        border-radius: 0 0.4rem 0.4rem 0;
      }
      .free-note strong { color: var(--ink); }

      ol.steps { padding-left: 1.25rem; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
      ol.steps li { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }

      /* The first objection a caregiver has is practical, not emotional: what
         does my parent need, is there an app, how long will this take me. That
         answer existed on this page but sat five hundred words down, under an
         essay, so it now sits directly beneath the call to action. */
      .setup {
        background: var(--bg-soft);
        border: 1px solid var(--line);
        border-radius: 0.9rem;
        padding: 1.5rem;
        margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
      }
      .setup h2 { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; font-size: 1.25rem; }
      .setup ol {
        list-style: none;
        counter-reset: step;
        display: grid;
        gap: 1.25rem;
        padding: 0;
        margin: 0;
      }
      .setup li {
        counter-increment: step;
        position: relative;
        padding-left: 2.5rem;
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.5;
      }
      .setup li::before {
        content: counter(step);
        position: absolute;
        left: 0;
        top: -0.1rem;
        width: 1.8rem;
        height: 1.8rem;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: var(--brand);
        color: #fff;
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
      }
      .setup-foot { margin: 1.25rem 0 0; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--muted); }

      @media (min-width: 40rem) {
        .setup ol { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1.5rem; }
      }

      .note {
        background: var(--bg-soft);
        border-left: 4px solid var(--brand);
        padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
        border-radius: 0 0.4rem 0.4rem 0;
        margin: 2rem 0;
      }

      footer {
        border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
        margin-top: 4rem;
        padding: 2rem 0 3rem;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 1rem;
      }
      footer a { color: var(--muted); }
      footer .links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }

      a { color: var(--brand); }

      .rule { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin: 3rem 0; }

      /* Product screenshots. The tinted panel does the work: a bare screenshot
         of a white app on a white page reads as part of the page rather than as
         a picture of something. The panel bleeds slightly wider than the text
         column so it registers as an image without breaking the measure. */
      .shot {
        margin: 2rem -1rem 2.5rem;
        padding: 1rem;
        background: var(--bg-soft);
        border-radius: 0.9rem;
      }
      .shot img {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        height: auto;
        border: 1px solid var(--line);
        border-radius: 0.6rem;
        box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgb(31 41 51 / 12%);
      }
      .shot figcaption {
        margin-top: 0.9rem;
        padding: 0 0.25rem;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.5;
      }

      @media (min-width: 48rem) {
        .shot { margin-left: -2rem; margin-right: -2rem; padding: 1.5rem; }
      }

      /* Blog */
      .post-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
      .post-list li { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
      .post-list h2 { margin-top: 0; }
      .post-list h2 a { text-decoration: none; }
      .post-list h2 a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
      .post-meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
      .post blockquote {
        margin: 1.5rem 0;
        padding-left: 1.25rem;
        border-left: 4px solid var(--line);
        color: var(--muted);
      }
      .post ul, .post ol { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
      .post li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }

      /* Comparison tables in posts. Without this a Markdown table renders with
         no padding at all and adjacent cells run into each other — "Change the
         schedule from anywhere no" reads as one phrase. */
      .post table {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        margin: 1.5rem 0;
        font-size: 1rem;
      }
      .post th, .post td {
        padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
        text-align: left;
        vertical-align: top;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      }
      .post th {
        border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
        font-weight: 700;
      }
      .post tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
      /* First column carries the row's label and needs the room. */
      .post td:first-child, .post th:first-child { width: 42%; }

      /* Mailing list */
      .subscribe {
        background: var(--bg-soft);
        border-radius: 0.6rem;
        padding: 1.5rem;
        margin: 3rem 0 1rem;
      }
      .subscribe h2 { margin-top: 0; }
      .subscribe-form label { display: block; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
      .subscribe-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; }
      .subscribe-row input {
        flex: 1 1 16rem;
        padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
        font: inherit;
        color: var(--ink);
        background: var(--bg);
        border: 2px solid var(--line);
        border-radius: 0.6rem;
      }
      .subscribe-row input:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--brand); outline-offset: 1px; }
      .subscribe-row button { cursor: pointer; font: inherit; }

      /* Off-screen rather than display:none — some bots skip hidden inputs. */
      .honeypot {
        position: absolute;
        left: -9999px;
        width: 1px;
        height: 1px;
        overflow: hidden;
      }

      /* Printable checklists. Boxes are drawn with a border rather than a
         real checkbox so they survive printing — form controls print
         inconsistently across browsers and some drop them entirely. */
      .checklist { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
      .checklist li {
        position: relative;
        padding: 0.35rem 0 0.35rem 2rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      }
      .checklist li::before {
        content: "";
        position: absolute;
        left: 0;
        top: 0.55rem;
        width: 1.05rem;
        height: 1.05rem;
        border: 2px solid var(--muted);
        border-radius: 0.2rem;
      }
      /* One row per item, one box per day — a daily checklist on a weekly
         sheet needs somewhere to record each day, not a single box that is
         used up on Monday. */
      .week-grid { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
      .week-grid th[scope="row"] { font-weight: 400; text-align: left; padding: 0.3rem 0.5rem 0.3rem 0; }
      .week-grid thead th { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); text-align: center; padding: 0 0.2rem 0.3rem; font-weight: 700; }
      .week-grid td { text-align: center; padding: 0.3rem 0.2rem; width: 2.2rem; }
      .week-grid tr { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
      .week-grid .box {
        display: inline-block;
        width: 1.05rem;
        height: 1.05rem;
        border: 2px solid var(--muted);
        border-radius: 0.2rem;
      }

      .sheet-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; }
      .sheet-week { margin: -0.5rem 0 1.5rem; }

      /* Printable routine sheet */
      .print-hint { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; }
      .sheet-title { margin-top: 0; }
      .sheet-heading { margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem; }
      .sheet-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
      .sheet-table th {
        text-align: left;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.05em;
        color: var(--muted);
        border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
        padding: 0.4rem 0.5rem;
      }
      .sheet-table td { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); height: 2.6rem; padding: 0.4rem 0.5rem; }
      .sheet-table .tick { width: 4rem; }
      .fill-name { display: inline-block; min-width: 12rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink); }
      /* Separate from fill-name so the two can be sized independently. */
      .fill-week { display: inline-block; min-width: 8rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink); }

      @media print {
        /* What prints is the sheet: no navigation, no calls to action, black on
           white regardless of what the screen was showing. */
        header, footer, .no-print { display: none !important; }
        body { background: #fff; color: #000; font-size: 12pt; }
        .wrap { max-width: none; padding: 0; }
        .sheet-table th { border-bottom: 2px solid #000; color: #000; }
        .sheet-table td { border-bottom: 1px solid #666; }
        .sheet-heading { page-break-after: avoid; }

        /* Density overrides are scoped to .sheet-dense, not global. The
           checklist needs them to fit a page; the routine sheet does not, and
           applying them there shrank its handwriting rows from 2.6rem to
           1.8rem — smaller boxes to write in, on a sheet whose whole purpose
           is being written on by hand. */
        .sheet-dense { font-size: 10.5pt; }
        .sheet-dense .sheet-title { margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
        .sheet-dense .sheet-week { margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
        .sheet-dense .sheet-note { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
        .sheet-dense .sheet-heading { margin: 0.9rem 0 0.3rem; }
        .sheet-dense .sheet-table td { height: 1.8rem; }
        .sheet-dense .checklist li { border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; page-break-inside: avoid; padding: 0.12rem 0 0.12rem 1.6rem; }
        .sheet-dense .checklist li::before { border-color: #000; top: 0.3rem; width: 0.85rem; height: 0.85rem; }
        .sheet-dense .week-grid th, .sheet-dense .week-grid td { padding: 0.08rem 0.2rem; }
        .sheet-dense .week-grid .box { width: 0.85rem; height: 0.85rem; }
        .sheet-dense .checklist { margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
        .week-grid .box { border-color: #000; }
      }

      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root {
          --ink: #e6e9ee;
          --muted: #a7b0bb;
          --line: #2c333d;
          --brand: #7f9cf5;
          --brand-dark: #a3b8f8;
          --bg: #14181e;
          --bg-soft: #1b212a;
        }
        /* --brand lightens in dark mode, so white text on it fails contrast.
           Same reason, same fix, for the numbered step markers. */
        .btn-primary { color: #14181e; }
        .setup li::before { color: #14181e; }
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <header>
      <div class="wrap">
        <%#
          The badge sits with the logo rather than being another line of copy,
          because someone who arrives on the FAQ or a blog post from a search
          could otherwise read three pages without ever learning it costs
          nothing. Stated once, quietly, on every page — the page that argues
          the point is /faq, which answers why.
        %>
        <span class="brand">
          <a class="logo" href="/">Remindly</a>
          <span class="badge-free">Free</span>
        </span>
        <%#
          Three links, not the footer's seven. Someone arriving on a blog post
          from a search previously had no visible route anywhere except Sign in
          — the one thing they are not ready to do. These are the "still
          deciding" path; privacy, terms and the printables stay in the footer
          where people go looking for them.

          No JavaScript menu: these pages ship none, and a hamburger would mean
          shipping some for three links. They wrap onto a second line on a
          narrow screen instead, which costs a little height and no complexity.
        %>
        <nav class="top-nav" aria-label="Main">
          <a href="<%= how_to_path %>">How it works</a>
          <a href="<%= faq_path %>">FAQ</a>
          <a href="<%= blog_path %>">Blog</a>
          <% if current_user %>
            <a class="nav-cta" href="<%= dashboard_path %>">Dashboard</a>
          <% else %>
            <a class="nav-cta" href="<%= login_path %>">Sign in</a>
          <% end %>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="wrap">
      <%= yield %>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="links">
          <a href="<%= how_to_path %>">How it works</a>
          <a href="<%= faq_path %>">FAQ</a>
          <a href="<%= caregiver_checklist_path %>">Free checklist</a>
          <a href="<%= blog_path %>">Blog</a>
          <a href="<%= privacy_path %>">Privacy</a>
          <a href="<%= terms_path %>">Terms</a>
          <% if current_user %>
            <a href="<%= dashboard_path %>">Dashboard</a>
          <% else %>
            <a href="<%= login_path %>">Sign in</a>
          <% end %>
          <a href="mailto:hello@remindly.care">hello@remindly.care</a>
        </div>
        <p>© <%= Date.current.year %> Remindly</p>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
